# Round 3 of the cone-cost campaign: the stage FUSION -- hand the 8-wide
# stages' outputs over in REGISTERS instead of through the six stack arrays
# (zLoArr/zHiArr/aliveLane, dzArr/invDzArr/fadeStartArr).
#
# BUILT, MEASURED, REJECTED. It is bit-exact (city 3cbe42b1 / greets 778fa6ac /
# fountain 8db68ccb all 3/3 with it on) and it does exactly what it claims --
# four of the solve's six `str q` disappear from the disassembly. It is still
# worth only 0.1% instructions, because the register allocator re-spends every
# register it frees, and it COSTS +2.0% instructions in the real two-arm
# shipping structure. Full numbers: docs/HW_PROFILING.md section 11.
#
# Kept as a patch rather than as #if arms in the kernel because it touches eight
# sites across 300 lines and leaving it in would cost the shipping binary the
# very 2% that disqualified it.
#
#   git apply scratchpad/cone_fuse.patch
#   cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="-DFDS_CONE_FUSE=1 -DFDS_CONE_FORCE=1"
#   # ...measure with scratchpad/cone_fuse_ab.sh, then: git checkout FDS/RENDER/DeferredVolumetric.cpp
#
